(ii) \(3 y(2 y-7)-3(y-4)-63=6 y^{2}-21 y-3 y+12-63\)
\[=6 y^{2}-24 y-51\]

For \(y=-2,6 y^{2}-24 y-51=6(-2)^{2}-24(-2)-51\)
\[\begin{aligned}
& =6 \times 4+24 \times 2-51 \\
& =24+48-51=72-51=21
\end{aligned}\]

Example 6: Add
(i) \(5 m(3-m)\) and \(6 m^{2}-13 m\)
(ii) \(4 y\left(3 y^{2}+5 y-7\right)\) and \(2\left(y^{3}-4 y^{2}+5\right)\)

\section*{Solution:}
(i) First expression \(=5 m(3-m)=(5 m \times 3)-(5 m \times m)=15 m-5 m^{2}\)

Now adding the second expression to it, \(15 m-5 m^{2}+6 m^{2}-13 m=m^{2}+2 m\)
(ii) The first expression \(=4 y\left(3 y^{2}+5 y-7\right)=\left(4 y \times 3 y^{2}\right)+(4 y \times 5 y)+(4 y \times(-7))\)
\[=12 y^{3}+20 y^{2}-28 y\]

The second expression \(=2\left(y^{3}-4 y^{2}+5\right)=2 y^{3}+2 \times\left(-4 y^{2}\right)+2 \times 5\)
\[=2 y^{3}-8 y^{2}+10\]

Adding the two expressions,
\[\begin{array}{rll}
12 y^{3} & +20 y^{2}-28 y & \\
+\quad 2 y^{3} & -8 y^{2} & +10 \\
\hline 14 y^{3} & +12 y^{2}-28 y & +10
\end{array}\]

Example 7: Subtract \(3 p q(p-q)\) from \(2 p q(p+q)\).
Solution: We have
\[\begin{aligned}
& 3 p q(p-q)=3 p^{2} q-3 p q^{2} \quad \text { and } \\
& 2 p q(p+q)=2 p^{2} q+2 p q^{2}
\end{aligned}\]

Subtracting,
\[\begin{aligned}
2 p^{2} q & +2 p q^{2} \\
3 p^{2} q & -3 p q^{2} \\
- & + \\
\hline-p^{2} q & +5 p q^{2}
\end{aligned}\]

