Example 1: The area of a trapezium shaped field is \(480 \mathrm{~m}^{2}\), the distance between two parallel sides is 15 m and one of the parallel side is 20 m . Find the other parallel side.
Solution: One of the parallel sides of the trapezium is \(a=20 \mathrm{~m}\), let another parallel side be \(b\), height \(h=15 \mathrm{~m}\).

The given area of trapezium \(=480 \mathrm{~m}^{2}\).
\[\begin{aligned}
\text { Area of a trapezium } & =\frac{1}{2} h(a+b) \\
\text { So } 480 & =\frac{1}{2} \times 15 \times(20+b) \text { or } \frac{480 \times 2}{15}=20+b \\
\text { or } 64 & =20+b \text { or } b=44 \mathrm{~m}
\end{aligned}\]

Hence the other parallel side of the trapezium is 44 m .

