\subsection*{9.5.3 Cylinder}

We know that volume of a cuboid can be found by finding the product of area of base and its height. Can we find the volume of a cylinder in the same way?
Just like cuboid, cylinder has got a top and a base which are
![](https://cdn.mathpix.com/cropped/2dba4960-d233-4c45-9dbe-6e0a59dba658-131.jpg?height=243&width=602&top_left_y=1430&top_left_x=1256)
