\subsection*{10.4 Use of Exponents to Express Small Numbers in Standard Form}

Observe the following facts.
1. The distance from the Earth to the Sun is \(149,600,000,000 \mathrm{~m}\).
2. The speed of light is \(300,000,000 \mathrm{~m} / \mathrm{sec}\).
